  "pitfalls": [
    "Overriding `clone()` without copying mutable fields shares lists and maps between copies.",
    "Handing out the registry's own prototype lets one caller corrupt every later copy.",
    "Deep-copying immutable values like `String` or records with immutable components wastes memory; share them."
  ],
  "quiz": {
    "q": "Same `Template` as `ShallowCloneBug`. What does this print?",
    "code": "Template a = new Template(\"A\");\na.addSection(\"x\");\nTemplate b = a.clone();\nb.setTitle(\"B\");\nb.addSection(\"y\");\nSystem.out.println(a);",
    "lang": "java",
    "options": [
      "A [x]",
      "B [x, y]",
      "A [x, y]",
      "B [x]"
    ],
    "answer": 2,
    "why": "`setTitle` replaces only the copy's own field. Both objects share one list, so adding `y` through `b` shows up in `a`."
  },
  "takeaway": "Copy a configured prototype; deep-copy mutable fields, share immutable ones.",
